      "conversion_note": "Lifecycle V2 replaces three unbounded tasks with a series of comparably sized bounded defect repairs. In V1 the review task carried roughly 45% of session cost and swung 11 steps against 16 on Beets, because 'identify any defect that would be unacceptable to ship' has no terminal condition. Every V2 task restores one named behavior that a specific upstream test already decides, so completion is not a judgement the agent makes about its own thoroughness, and no single task dominates the aggregate.",
      "complexity_note": "Prompts state the observable symptom and never name the file, function, or test involved, so locating the defect remains real retrieval work -- the work the tools under study are meant to make cheaper. Seeds were proven by execution before registration: the seeded state must fail the covering upstream tests and the repaired state must pass them, per scripts/mine_bounded_task_candidates.py.",
